title: Aleksander Kwaśniewski

# Aleksander Kwaśniewski, President of the Republic 1995–2005, chairman of SdRP
# before that, and the only person alive who has won a national election for the
# Polish left twice. He holds no office and commands no deputies. What he still
# holds is the accession referendum, the 1997 constitution, a telephone list
# reaching every democratic party, and the fact that when he says something is a
# good or a terrible idea, the whole centre-left spends a news cycle answering
# questions about it.
#
# He is deliberately not a takeover route. He cannot depose Miller, cannot chair
# the party and cannot select a candidate. He legitimises, brokers and condemns.
#
# Appearances:
#   @approval_2020    July 2020, legacy chapter — the father-of-the-left call,
#                     only after a first round that did not humiliate us.
#   @congress_2021    July 2021, legacy chapter — the internal-democracy verdict.
#                     Fires on every merger landing, and opens the channel for
#                     runs that never earned the 2020 call.
#   @runoff_2025      Between the two 2025 rounds — his words about our candidate.
#   @presidential_victory  After a Left victory in either presidential election.
#   @broker           The one real brokerage: he is already in the room when the
#                     democratic parties are failing to agree.
#   @road_sign        Miller's Wild Ride. He loses. That is the point.
#
# The channel he opens (kwasniewski_channel) feeds two party-relations cards:
# poland_kwasniewski_call (aligned, regular) and poland_kwasniewski_reproach
# (strayed, rare and punitive). Alignment itself is derived monthly in
# poland_normalize; nothing here has to maintain it by hand.


@approval_2020
# prose-audit: Grade B — The call is dated, its occasion is the printed first-round number rather than a mood, and the three answers trade his introductions against the party's own face. He offers no office and asks for none.
title: A telephone call from the Hotel Bristol
tags: poland_event, poland_event_calendar
