Q.kwasniewski_2020_done = 1;
Q.kwasniewski_channel = 1;
Q.kwasniewski_verdict =
    "Approved the 2020 first round: " +
    String(Q.pres_performance_band || "a result the left could defend");
Q.news_headline =
    "Kwaśniewski calls the Left's first round the best the left has had since he left office";
!}

= July 2020 — The father of the left would like a word

**Aleksander Kwaśniewski**, President of the Republic from 1995 to 2005, has no
office, no party card and no deputies. He has an apartment, a foundation, a
speaking calendar and the telephone numbers of every person who has led a
democratic party in this country since 1989. He is also the last person to win
a national election for the Polish left, and he has never once let anyone
forget it.

He has read the count. **[+ presidential_candidate +]** took **[+
pres_r1_display_left +]%** — [+ pres_performance_band +]. Kwaśniewski's own
party ran Magdalena Ogórek in 2015 and took 2.38%, the worst number the left
has ever put on a presidential ballot, and he has spent five years being asked
about it at every book fair in the country.

So he is generous, and he is not subtle about the price of the generosity. He
would like the Left to consolidate, modernise, stop treating the European
question as somebody else's argument, and stop mistaking its own internal
quarrels for politics. He would like to say so, warmly, on television, with our
candidate's name in the sentence.

[? if left_in_government: He mentions, without emphasis, that he knows what a
governing left costs its own activists.?][? if not left_in_government: He
mentions, without emphasis, that opposition is where he built everything he
later spent.?]

- @approval_take
- @approval_polite
- @approval_refuse

@approval_take
title: Take the endorsement, the introductions and the photograph
subtitle: The old electorate and the democratic parties both hear it. So does everyone in the party who joined after 2019.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 3;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 4;
Q.pensioner_support += 3;
Q.urban_progressive_support += 2;
Q.ko_relation += 4;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.barons_strength += 2;
Q.barons_dissent -= 3;
Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
Q.razem_dissent += 4;
Q.news_headline =
    "Kwaśniewski endorses the Left's campaign and opens his own telephone list to it";
!}

He does it properly: an hour of television, a paragraph that quotes our
candidate's actual programme, and four telephone calls afterwards that we did
not have to make ourselves. Editors who had stopped returning our press office's
messages return them within the week.

Razem's organisers point out that the man being thanked signed the 1997
constitution's compromise on church funding, sent troops to Iraq and left office
with the party he built in ruins. Both things are true. Only one of them is
worth a fortnight of coverage.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@approval_polite
title: Accept the good wishes and keep the campaign's own face
subtitle: The relationship is real and unspent; the party is not photographed standing behind a former president.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 1;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 2;
Q.party_unity += 3;
Q.progressive_credibility += 3;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.pensioner_support += 1;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 2;
Q.razem_dissent -= 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left thanks Kwaśniewski and keeps its own candidate at the front of its campaign";
!}

We thank him, we mean it, and we do not put him on the poster. The party that
came out of 2019 is not asking a president of the 1990s to explain what it is
for, and the people who joined it after the Women's Strike notice that we did
not.

He is unbothered — he has been managing his own reputation longer than most of
our club has been alive — and the line stays open.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@approval_refuse
title: Say plainly that the Third Republic is not our reference point
subtitle: A clean generational break. He does not stop taking our calls; he simply starts describing us differently.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing -= 2;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias -= 6;
Q.progressive_credibility += 5;
Q.young_support += 2;
Q.razem_dissent -= 4;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 3;
Q.barons_dissent += 7;
Q.pensioner_support -= 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 3;
Q.public_trust -= 1;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left declines a former president's blessing and says why in public";
!}

We answer that the transformation he presided over produced the towns our
organisers now canvass, that his generation's settlement with the Church is the
reason a woman cannot get a legal termination in this country, and that a left
which needs his permission has not been rebuilt at all.

He takes it in good humour in public. In private, the old SLD county chairmen
are told which of their two parties just insulted the last man to win them
anything, and he begins, from here on, to describe us to journalists rather than
to speak for us.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue


