= [+ year +] — A call no Polish Left candidate has received in a generation

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Robert Biedroń": Before the concession
calls are finished, **Aleksander Kwaśniewski** telephones **Robert Biedroń** and
congratulates Wiosna's founder on becoming Poland's first openly gay
President-elect. A campaign once treated as an exercise in visibility has won
the office, and Kwaśniewski says plainly that the victory belongs to Biedroń,
not to the older men now arriving for the photograph.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Robert Biedroń": On camera he explicitly
endorses Biedroń's presidency as a mandate for European Poland, civil equality
and local government that can be felt outside Warsaw. Former SLD voters hear a
recognisable democratic left; Wiosna organisers hear the last president of the
old party admit that its successor came through a movement he did not build.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg": **Aleksander
Kwaśniewski** calls **Adrian Zandberg** before either camp has found a version
of the moment that makes their old arguments disappear. He congratulates the
Razem co-founder who spent years putting the transformation, Iraq and the
Third Republic's social settlement on trial — and does not ask him to withdraw
a word of it.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg": His televised
endorsement is therefore worth more than reconciliation theatre. Kwaśniewski
endorses Zandberg's mandate on wages, housing and public investment while
calling the constitutional and European inheritance common ground. Razem's
organisers hear a founder of the old order acknowledge that the next Left
presidency can be built by its most disciplined critic.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": The first
call reaches **Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk** among campaign staff still carrying
folders on wages, schools and the labour inspectorate. **Aleksander
Kwaśniewski** congratulates her on making public services — the machinery that
turns formal freedom into a usable life — the substance of a winning
presidential campaign.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": He then
explicitly endorses Dziemianowicz-Bąk as a social-democratic President who can
measure every signature by what it does at work and in a public institution.
[? if year = 2020: A primary choice that looked generational has become a
national mandate.?][? if year = 2025: Her record of delivery and coalition
compromise has been tested by the whole electorate and survived.?] The old
party's language of modernisation is being handed to a winner who defines it
through labour and care.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Anna-Maria Żukowska": **Aleksander
Kwaśniewski** congratulates **Anna-Maria Żukowska** as an heir to the SLD
political tradition who reached the Palace without adopting its preference for
quiet sentences. The combative interviews, parliamentary arguments and clips
her critics called undisciplined have produced a national majority.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Anna-Maria Żukowska": His endorsement
is explicit and notably free of advice about sounding more presidential.
Kwaśniewski says Żukowska has her own mandate to defend a secular state, equal
citizenship and Poland's European place. The old apparatus gets continuity;
the candidate gets recognition without being asked to become its museum.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Katarzyna Kotula": **Aleksander
Kwaśniewski** calls **Katarzyna Kotula** in a room filled less by former
ministers than by equality organisers, Women's Strike veterans and people who
learned politics through Wiosna. He congratulates her on turning movements the
Palace once received as petitioners into the coalition that will occupy it.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Katarzyna Kotula": On television he
explicitly endorses Kotula's mandate for bodily autonomy, civil equality and a
secular republic. The constitution signed during his presidency is now being
entrusted to a President-elect who has spent her career demanding that its
promise of equal citizenship become ordinary state practice.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat": **Aleksander
Kwaśniewski** congratulates **Magdalena Biejat** after a campaign that made
housing, care and the cost of an ordinary household presidential questions.
[? if year = 2020: A Razem deputy who entered the primary as a bridge between
currents has crossed the whole electoral field.?][? if year = 2025: The deputy
marshal of the Senate has converted patient institutional work into a national
majority.?] He calls that an achievement of substance rather than tone.?]

[? if kwasniewski_victory_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat": His public
endorsement names the programme: homes people can afford, care the state does
not leave to women for free, and institutions used without reverence or
contempt. Older social democrats hear their promise of security renewed;
younger organisers hear Kwaśniewski recognise a presidency built through
cooperation without surrender.?]

- @presidential_victory_continue

