= July 2021 — The room you did not know you were expected in

The invitation is mundane to the point of rudeness: a time, an address, no
subject. **Aleksander Kwaśniewski** does not schedule press conferences to
discuss the internal affairs of a party he left in 1995. He schedules coffee,
and then the coffee is on the front page of *Gazeta Wyborcza* by Thursday.

[? if kwasniewski_congress_face = "condemn": He has read the settlement. He
wants to know, in a tone he has used on prime ministers, whether anybody in our
leadership has considered what a party looks like from outside when its
constitutional disputes are resolved by removing the losing side's committee
posts. **[+ kwasniewski_congress_target +]**, he observes, has built a machine
that works. So did the one he inherited in 1993. It delivered two terms and
then 2015, and there was nothing left of it because nobody inside it had ever
been allowed to win an argument.?]
[? if kwasniewski_congress_face = "approve": He has read the settlement, and he
is — visibly, irritatingly — impressed. A Polish left party has resolved a
leadership fight by counting its own members instead of by changing the locks.
He points out that SdRP never once did this, that SLD never once did this, and
that he is therefore in a position to know how rare it is.?]
[? if kwasniewski_congress_face = "scold": He has read the settlement, or rather
he has tried to. He would like to know which organisation he is supposed to
telephone when he wants to speak to the Polish left, and whether that answer
will still be correct in a year. He is not angry. He is doing the thing that is
worse, which is finding it funny.?]

He is careful, throughout, to say that he has no standing to instruct anybody.
He is equally careful to say all of it where it can be quoted.

- @congress_concede
- @congress_answer
- @congress_break

@congress_concede
title: Fly to him and concede a written appeals procedure
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Reopens part of the settlement: published grounds, a member appeal and a time limit on any suspension.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is no money for a negotiation nobody has demanded of us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 3;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 6;
if (
    String(Q.left_mandate || "") == "disciplinary" ||
    String(Q.left_mandate || "") == "administrative"
) {
    Q.left_mandate = "negotiated_truce";
    Q.merger_resolution = "Settlement reopened under an appeals procedure";
}
Q.party_unity += 5;
Q.public_trust += 3;
Q.institutional_trust += 2;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 4;
Q.razem_dissent -= 3;
Q.pps_dissent -= 3;
Q.barons_dissent += 6;
Q.barons_strength -= 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left publishes an appeals procedure after a former president's intervention";
!}

We go to him, which is itself the concession, and we come back with something
narrow and real: no suspension without published grounds, a member appeal that
has to be answered inside sixty days, and an automatic expiry on any measure
taken between congresses. Nobody's chairmanship changes.

The apparatus understands exactly what has happened. A man with no office and no
votes has just rewritten a party statute because the alternative was two weeks of
being asked about it on television. That is a precedent about who our leadership
answers to, and the people who lost this round will file it.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@congress_answer
title: Answer him in public, on our own terms
subtitle: Free. Defend the settlement as ours to make, agree with him about Europe, and refuse the lecture on internal discipline.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing += 1;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias += 1;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.party_unity += 1;
Q.progressive_credibility += 1;
if (Q.kwasniewski_congress_face == "condemn") {
    Q.public_trust -= 1;
    Q.barons_dissent -= 2;
} else {
    Q.public_trust += 1;
}
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left answers Kwaśniewski in public and concedes nothing on the statute";
!}

We do the interview he was always going to force us into, and we do it well. We
agree with him about Europe, the courts and the accession settlement, because we
do. We tell him that a party which has just spent a year merging three
organisations is entitled to decide its own rules, and that the last leadership
which took his advice about internal discipline is the one that produced the
2015 result.

He enjoys it. That is the risk of answering him: an argument with Kwaśniewski is
an argument conducted on a stage he built, and every minute of it is a minute
about him.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue

@congress_break
title: Tell the salon of the Third Republic that it has no jurisdiction here
subtitle: Free, loud, and permanent in his memory. The party's own left applauds; the old electorate and the democratic parties do not.
on-arrival: {!
Q.kwasniewski_standing -= 3;
Q.kwasniewski_alignment_bias -= 10;
Q.kwasniewski_reproach_debt += 1;
Q.progressive_credibility += 4;
Q.young_support += 2;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 3;
Q.razem_dissent -= 3;
Q.party_unity += 2;
Q.pensioner_support -= 3;
Q.urban_progressive_support -= 2;
Q.ko_relation -= 5;
Q.public_trust -= 3;
Q.institutional_trust -= 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left tells a former president that the salon of the Third Republic has no jurisdiction over it";
!}

We say it on the record: the Round Table generation negotiated a state, sold its
industry, financed its Church and lost its own party, and it does not now get to
audit the people rebuilding what it left. The clip is everywhere within a day.
Our organisers love it. So do Konfederacja's.

What it actually costs is not the argument, which we win, but the address book.
Every democratic party in the country has just watched us decide that the
warmest available intermediary between all of us is an obstacle. The next time
we need someone to sit in a room and make an agreement easier, we will be doing
it alone.

- @poland_event_queue: Continue


